    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d202">

                <pb facs="0378" n="316" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg316"/>

                <head>No. 197.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Welsh to Mr. Evarts</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-11-09"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 9, 1878</date>.
                        (Received November 20.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 158.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I received late in the evening of the 7th
                    instant Lord Salisbury’s reply to your dispatch No. 145, of the 27th of
                    September, relating to the award of the Halifax commision. I sent you by cable
                    yesterday, in cipher, such an abstract of this paper as the limited time allowed
                    us enabled us to prepare, and I now inclose herewith two printed copies of the
                    letters, for which we are indebted to the courtesy of the foreign office.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN WELSH.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d202-a1.xml" xpointer="d202-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
